  "id": "nodal-point",
  "term": "nodal point",
  "definition": "In this historical optics usage, the nodal point is the reference point in the “reduced” eye through which a straight line from a luminous point is drawn and extended to the retina. It serves to determine where that light source is represented on the retina.",
